{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"LLM-Review ps2 = BLOCK (-1). Blocking (correctness): the AC5 comment claimed recovered was un-folded from applied, but on the real cutover path mutations_applied still included recovered (double-count vs the new mutations_recovered field). Root cause: derive_pass_tally's applied is the LEGACY folded count — build_pass_tally sets applied_count=applied+recovered (pinned by test_build_pass_tally_folds_recovered_into_applied) and the non-error manifest count includes recovered outcomes. Fix (ps3, reconcile.py only — build_pass_tally's fold is an intentional legacy-consumer contract left intact): mutations_applied = max(0, tally['applied'] - recovered_count), un-folding downstream so the five reported buckets are DISJOINT and sum to mutation_count (AC5 exact tallies). RED-first: test_mixed_pass_tally_is_exact_including_recovered rewritten to the production-folded shape (applied_count 9 = 4 applied + 5 recovered) asserting mutations_applied==4 + exactness; NEW test_reconcile_unfolds_the_real_build_pass_tally_fold drives a real CutoverReport through build_pass_tally into reconcile (addresses the advisory that the old test used a synthetic independent shape). Both seen RED (5==3) then GREEN. Regression: tests/unit/rebar_reconciler + interfaces/facades + interfaces/contracts = 4558 passed/2 skipped; lint+typecheck green; reconcile 798 LOC (<800)."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787736508391309001,"uuid":"78bf2134-26e5-48ca-ac9b-3eeefddd3e05"}